    {
      "id": "scene-2-definition",
      "type": "text",
      "heading": "The Core Concept",
      "content": "In a right-angled triangle, the square of the hypotenuse is equal to the sum of the squares of the other two sides.",
      "durationInSeconds": 6,
      "layout": "split"
    },
    {
      "id": "scene-3-formula",
      "type": "math",
      "heading": "The Formula",
      "content": "a^{2} + b^{2} = c^{2}",
      "durationInSeconds": 5,
      "layout": "centered"
    },
    {
      "id": "scene-4-anatomy",
      "type": "point_list",
      "heading": "Defining the Components",
      "items": [
        "Sides \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) are called the legs.",
        "Side \\(c\\) is the hypotenuse.",
        "The hypotenuse is always the longest side.",
        "It is always opposite the 90-degree angle."
      ],
      "durationInSeconds": 8,
      "layout": "split"
    },
    {
      "id": "scene-5-example-setup",
      "type": "math",
      "heading": "Example: Find the Hypotenuse",
      "content": "\\text{Given: } a = 3, b = 4, c = ?",
      "durationInSeconds": 5,
      "layout": "top"
    },
    {
      "id": "scene-6-example-calc",
      "type": "math",
      "heading": "Step-by-Step Calculation",
      "content": "3^{2} + 4^{2} = c^{2} \\\\ 9 + 16 = c^{2} \\\\ 25 = c^{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{25} = c \\\\ c = 5",
      "durationInSeconds": 10,
      "layout": "centered"
    },
    {
      "id": "scene-7-summary",
      "type": "point_list",
      "heading": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
